      "title": "Routing attempts by outcome",
      "description": "Every provider considered, by how the attempt ended. `served` is the happy path; `refused` is a provider that was asked and said no; `breaker_open` is one the router did not bother asking; `shed` is a recovering provider whose ramp did not admit this request.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "switchyard-prom"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 8,
        "y": 11,
        "w": 8,
